#==============================================================================================
#
#   point - Example of a native module with a class: Point, with getters, setters, a method
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of QuickJS's examples/point.c, the native module examples/test_point.js imports
#       (as "./point.so"): a class Point(x, y) whose instances hold a native PointData, with
#       the accessors x and y (one getter and one setter told apart by their magic) and
#       the method norm(). Subclassing works because the constructor takes the prototype
#       from new_target. An embedder links it in and registers it with
#       host.js_register_native_module("point", point.js_init_module), as ljs does.
#
#       QuickJS: Example of C module with a class
#
#       Copyright (c) 2019 Fabrice Bellard
